    },
    "reason": "Ordinary eager and compiled BF16 Multiply flushed tiny operands even when the finite f32 product is normal. OP2 now reuses existing protected low_product; other shader operations unchanged."
  },
  "notes": [
    "Typed transport preserves checked MlxLowTensor wrappers; legacy run remains f32-only and rejects other signatures before tracing.",
    "Eager and compiled casts, low arithmetic, low reductions and direct low matmul share generic lowering recipes and the raw operation/custom Metal emitter.",
    "Program owns prepared kernels/constants; native payload only borrows handles and owns plain metadata. No reentrant Api::call or global compile/default-device changes.",
    "Enabled native replay preserves internal low-rounding boundaries and raw storage bits across changed input strides. Externally disabled mode remains correct.",
    "Only low_binary.metal OP2 changed among prior Metal sources; it preserves normal products involving BF16 subnormal inputs, with separate before/after evidence.",
    "Runtime lifetime and C-boundary error recovery tested; no sanitizer, allocator-leak measurement or typed-program performance claim.",
    "Benchmark source included; README outside this frozen executable source set."
  ],
